From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Windows SDK 26100 compatibility (Micromium)

Chromium 153 pins Windows SDK 10.0.28000.0 (Insider-only at the time of
writing) in three places and targets NTDDI_WIN11_BR throughout. This patch
retargets the Windows build at the public 10.0.26100.0 SDK so stock
VS2022 + public SDK builds work out of the box:

- build/toolchain/win/setup_toolchain.py + build/vs_toolchain.py:
  SDK_VERSION 28000 -> 26100 (the two files document that these pins must
  stay in sync; both are updated together here).
- build/config/win/BUILD.gn (winver config): NTDDI_VERSION WIN11_BR ->
  WIN11_GE (the highest level SDK 26100 defines), plus an explicit
  NTDDI_WIN11_BR=0x0A000011 define because base/win/windows_version.cc
  hard-gates on that macro existing.

Proven by a full local `autoninja chrome` build (Windows x64, VS 17.14
MSVC 19.44, SDK 26100): 33k+ targets compile and chrome.exe links and
renders. If upstream code ever uses a genuinely-28000-only SDK API, the
failing TU names it and this patch gets revisited.

Rebased against Chromium 153.0.8010.27 (branch 1681091).

--- a/build/toolchain/win/setup_toolchain.py
+++ b/build/toolchain/win/setup_toolchain.py
@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@
 import gn_helpers
 
 SCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(__file__)
-SDK_VERSION = '10.0.28000.0'
+# Micromium (Windows): build against the public 26100 SDK; upstream pins
+# 10.0.28000.0 (Insider-only at the time of writing). See windows/README.md.
+SDK_VERSION = '10.0.26100.0'
 MSVC_DIR = re.compile('^.*/VC/Tools/MSVC/[^/]+/include$')
 WINDOWS_KITS_DIR = re.compile(r'^(.*/Windows Kits/\d+/Include/[^/]+)/.*')
--- a/build/vs_toolchain.py
+++ b/build/vs_toolchain.py
@@ -62,4 +62,5 @@
 TOOLCHAIN_HASH = '3bfcb536c8'
-SDK_VERSION = '10.0.28000.0'
+# Micromium (Windows): must stay in sync with setup_toolchain.py (26100).
+SDK_VERSION = '10.0.26100.0'
 
 # Visual Studio versions are listed in descending order of priority.
--- a/build/config/win/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/win/BUILD.gn
@@ -307,4 +307,8 @@
   defines = [
-    "NTDDI_VERSION=NTDDI_WIN11_BR",
+    # Micromium (Windows): target the public 26100 SDK instead of the
+    # pinned 28000 SDK (Insider-only). NTDDI_WIN11_BR is defined manually
+    # because base/win/windows_version.cc gates on it. See windows/README.md.
+    "NTDDI_VERSION=NTDDI_WIN11_GE",
+    "NTDDI_WIN11_BR=0x0A000011",
 
     # We can't say `=_WIN32_WINNT_WIN10` here because some files do
